## 🗂️ File Organization

### Directory Structure
Follow these conventions:

```
app/
├── Events/
│   ├── Traits/           # Shared event behaviors
│   ├── SomethingCreated.php
│   └── SomethingUpdated.php
├── States/
│   └── SomethingState.php
├── Models/
│   └── Something.php     # Read-only projections
├── Livewire/
│   ├── Actions/          # Component actions
│   ├── Forms/           # Form objects
│   ├── CreateSomethingPage.php
│   └── ManageSomethingPage.php
├── DTOs/                # Data transfer objects
└── Queries/             # Complex read queries
```

### Naming Conventions
- Events: `SomethingHappened` (past tense)
- States: `SomethingState`
- Models: `Something`
- Livewire: `SomethingPage` or `SomethingComponent`

## 🔍 Common Patterns

### Creating Related Entities
When creating entities with relationships:

```php
public static function fromTemplate($params)
{
    // Main entity
    $id = MainEntityCreated::fire($params)->entity_id;
    Verbs::commit();

    $entity = self::find($id);

    // Related entities
    RelatedEntityCreated::fire([
        'main_entity_id' => $entity->id,
        // other params
    ]);

    return $entity;
}
```

### Handling Collections in States
```php
class SomeState extends State
{
    public Collection $item_ids;

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this->item_ids = collect();
    }

    public function items(): Collection
    {
        return $this->item_ids->map(fn ($id) => ItemState::load($id));
    }
}
```

### Validation in Events
```php
public function validate()
{
    $this->assert($this->start_date <= $this->end_date, 'Start date must not be after end date');
    $this->assert($this->rate_in_cents > 0, 'Rate must be positive');
}
```

## 🚨 Common Pitfalls to Avoid

### DON'T DO THESE THINGS:

1. **Direct model manipulation:**
```php
// WRONG
User::create(['name' => 'John']);
$user->update(['name' => 'Jane']);

// RIGHT
UserCreated::fire(name: 'John');
UserNameChanged::fire(user_id: $user->id, name: 'Jane');
```

2. **Skipping Verbs::commit():**
```php
// WRONG - events won't persist
$id = SomethingCreated::fire($data)->some_id;
return Something::find($id); // Will be null!

// RIGHT
$id = SomethingCreated::fire($data)->some_id;
Verbs::commit();
return Something::find($id);
```

3. **Testing without event setup:**
```php
// WRONG
$user = User::factory()->create();

// RIGHT
$user = $this->createUser();
```

4. **Complex logic in Livewire components:**
```php
// WRONG - business logic in component
public function save()
{
    $this->engagement->start_date = $this->start_date;
    $this->engagement->save();
    // ... complex logic
}

// RIGHT - delegate to model
public function save()
{
    $this->engagement->updateDates($this->start_date, $this->end_date);
}
```

